1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,709
What's today's video about? It's a summary of N4 grammar!

2
00:00:07,709 --> 00:00:09,209
Scene 1: Train Delays Due to Snow

3
00:00:09,209 --> 00:00:11,642
You're late.

4
00:00:11,665 --> 00:00:14,065
I'm sorry.

5
00:00:14,088 --> 00:00:16,354
What happened?

6
00:00:16,377 --> 00:00:19,611
The train was delayed.

7
00:00:19,634 --> 00:00:21,767
I see.

8
00:00:21,790 --> 00:00:23,590
Yeah.

9
00:00:23,613 --> 00:00:25,580
Was there an accident?

10
00:00:25,603 --> 00:00:29,822
No, it snowed.

11
00:00:29,845 --> 00:00:32,011
Snow?

12
00:00:32,034 --> 00:00:36,316
Yeah, it snowed a lot.

13
00:00:36,340 --> 00:00:38,907
That must have been tough.

14
00:00:38,929 --> 00:00:43,463
Yes, it was really cold.

15
00:00:43,486 --> 00:00:46,021
Did you catch a cold?

16
00:00:46,044 --> 00:00:50,090
No, I'm fine.

17
00:00:50,114 --> 00:00:52,119
That's good.

18
00:00:52,142 --> 00:00:54,799
Sorry to keep you waiting.

19
00:00:54,822 --> 00:00:57,389
Don't worry about it.

20
00:00:57,412 --> 00:00:59,283
Thank you.

21
00:00:59,307 --> 00:01:03,240
Has the meeting started yet?

22
00:01:03,263 --> 00:01:06,297
No, not yet.

23
00:01:06,320 --> 00:01:08,526
That's a relief.

24
00:01:08,549 --> 00:01:11,916
Yeah, I feel better now.

25
00:01:11,939 --> 00:01:15,217
Did you bring the documents?

26
00:01:15,240 --> 00:01:18,440
Oh, I forgot them.

27
00:01:18,463 --> 00:01:21,676
You forgot?

28
00:01:21,700 --> 00:01:25,512
Yeah, I was in a hurry.

29
00:01:25,536 --> 00:01:28,070
Are you going back to get them?

30
00:01:28,094 --> 00:01:31,929
No, I have the data.

31
00:01:31,953 --> 00:01:34,442
On your laptop?

32
00:01:34,465 --> 00:01:37,923
Yes, it's fine.

33
00:01:37,947 --> 00:01:46,956
You can download today's video script from the description and top comment. Please leave a comment before downloading!

34
00:01:46,956 --> 00:01:48,456
Scene 2: The View from My New Room

35
00:01:48,456 --> 00:01:52,223
Is this your new room?

36
00:01:52,246 --> 00:01:55,979
Yes, it is.

37
00:01:56,002 --> 00:01:58,202
It's spacious!

38
00:01:58,225 --> 00:02:02,392
Yeah, I can live here alone.

39
00:02:02,415 --> 00:02:05,188
The window is huge!

40
00:02:05,211 --> 00:02:09,064
You can see the mountains from there.

41
00:02:09,088 --> 00:02:11,654
Wow, really?

42
00:02:11,677 --> 00:02:14,644
You can even see Mt. Fuji.

43
00:02:14,668 --> 00:02:16,944
That's amazing!

44
00:02:16,967 --> 00:02:19,734
Can you see the ocean too?

45
00:02:19,757 --> 00:02:23,690
No, you can't see the ocean.

46
00:02:23,713 --> 00:02:26,246
I see.

47
00:02:26,269 --> 00:02:30,236
Can you see the stars at night?

48
00:02:30,259 --> 00:02:34,059
Yes, you can see a lot of them.

49
00:02:34,082 --> 00:02:36,482
This is a great room!

50
00:02:36,505 --> 00:02:40,872
But it's a little noisy.

51
00:02:40,895 --> 00:02:43,061
Why's that?

52
00:02:43,084 --> 00:02:46,618
I can hear a car.

53
00:02:46,641 --> 00:02:49,774
Yes, I can hear it.

54
00:02:49,797 --> 00:02:53,269
Can you hear the train too?

55
00:02:53,293 --> 00:02:56,660
No, I can't.

56
00:02:56,683 --> 00:02:59,483
That's good.

57
00:02:59,506 --> 00:03:03,594
Is there a place to shop nearby?

58
00:03:03,617 --> 00:03:07,350
Yes, there's a supermarket.

59
00:03:07,373 --> 00:03:09,827
Can I walk there?

60
00:03:09,851 --> 00:03:13,684
Yes, it's just a five-minute walk.

61
00:03:13,707 --> 00:03:15,787
That's convenient!

62
00:03:15,810 --> 00:03:18,853
You can cook here too.

63
00:03:18,877 --> 00:03:21,643
The kitchen is spacious, isn't it?

64
00:03:21,666 --> 00:03:25,466
Yes, it's very easy to use.

65
00:03:25,489 --> 00:03:32,594
The link to review today's video is in the description and top comment. *Note: The site may be deleted without notice.

66
00:03:32,594 --> 00:03:34,094
Scene 3: Busy Weekdays and a Relaxing Weekend

67
00:03:34,094 --> 00:03:37,428
This week has been so busy.

68
00:03:37,451 --> 00:03:41,251
Yes, extremely busy.

69
00:03:41,275 --> 00:03:44,367
Are you working overtime every day?

70
00:03:44,390 --> 00:03:47,676
Yeah, every single day.

71
00:03:47,700 --> 00:03:49,758
That sounds tough.

72
00:03:49,782 --> 00:03:53,982
I’ve been eating while working.

73
00:03:54,005 --> 00:03:56,844
That’s not good for you.

74
00:03:56,868 --> 00:03:58,961
I know.

75
00:03:58,984 --> 00:04:02,069
Do you listen to music while working?

76
00:04:02,093 --> 00:04:04,534
No, I don’t.

77
00:04:04,557 --> 00:04:07,324
Are you taking the weekend off?

78
00:04:07,347 --> 00:04:10,114
Yes, I plan to.

79
00:04:10,136 --> 00:04:12,203
What will you do?

80
00:04:12,226 --> 00:04:16,026
I’ll watch movies and drink.

81
00:04:16,049 --> 00:04:17,690
That sounds nice.

82
00:04:17,713 --> 00:04:20,886
I want to go to that restaurant.

83
00:04:20,910 --> 00:04:23,510
The one in front of the station?

84
00:04:23,533 --> 00:04:27,333
Yes, there’s always a line.

85
00:04:27,356 --> 00:04:29,807
It must be popular.

86
00:04:29,830 --> 00:04:34,263
Yeah, it’s cheap and delicious.

87
00:04:34,286 --> 00:04:36,491
I’d love to go too.

88
00:04:36,514 --> 00:04:39,247
Want to go together?

89
00:04:39,270 --> 00:04:42,937
I’d like to, but I don’t have time.

90
00:04:42,960 --> 00:04:44,793
Why's that?

91
00:04:44,816 --> 00:04:48,894
I have to clean and do laundry.

92
00:04:48,918 --> 00:04:51,407
You’re busy too, huh?

93
00:04:51,431 --> 00:04:55,049
Yeah, I’ve got so much to do.

94
00:04:55,072 --> 00:04:57,524
Let’s go another time.

95
00:04:57,548 --> 00:04:59,800
Yes, definitely.

96
00:04:59,823 --> 00:05:02,043
I’m looking forward to it!

97
00:05:02,066 --> 00:05:03,566
Scene 4: Handling Forgotten Items

98
00:05:03,566 --> 00:05:06,766
Oh no!

99
00:05:06,789 --> 00:05:09,231
What happened?

100
00:05:09,254 --> 00:05:12,687
I left my bag behind.

101
00:05:12,710 --> 00:05:15,593
Where did you leave it?

102
00:05:15,617 --> 00:05:19,819
I left it on the train.

103
00:05:19,843 --> 00:05:22,776
That must be tough.

104
00:05:22,799 --> 00:05:25,466
What should we do?

105
00:05:25,489 --> 00:05:28,622
Let's ask the station attendant.

106
00:05:28,645 --> 00:05:31,411
Okay, I'll do that.

107
00:05:31,434 --> 00:05:33,812
What kind of bag is it?

108
00:05:33,836 --> 00:05:36,735
It's a black bag.

109
00:05:36,758 --> 00:05:40,392
What's inside it?

110
00:05:40,415 --> 00:05:44,381
There's a wallet inside.

111
00:05:44,404 --> 00:05:46,890
Are there keys inside too?

112
00:05:46,914 --> 00:05:49,914
Yes, there are.

113
00:05:49,937 --> 00:05:53,170
Did you leave it on the seat?

114
00:05:53,193 --> 00:05:57,246
No, I put it on the overhead rack.

115
00:05:57,269 --> 00:06:00,962
You left it on the overhead rack, huh?

116
00:06:00,985 --> 00:06:04,919
Yeah, I got off without taking it.

117
00:06:04,942 --> 00:06:08,175
I'm sure it'll be found soon.

118
00:06:08,198 --> 00:06:10,467
I'm worried.

119
00:06:10,491 --> 00:06:14,180
The station attendant is calling about it now.

120
00:06:14,203 --> 00:06:16,886
Did they find it?

121
00:06:16,909 --> 00:06:20,182
They said the bag was found.

122
00:06:20,206 --> 00:06:22,382
That's good.

123
00:06:22,406 --> 00:06:25,047
That's a relief!

124
00:06:25,070 --> 00:06:28,108
I'll go pick it up now.

125
00:06:28,131 --> 00:06:32,377
Oh no, did you lose your ticket too?

126
00:06:32,400 --> 00:06:36,251
Oh, I don’t have my ticket either.

127
00:06:36,275 --> 00:06:40,242
Check your pockets carefully.

128
00:06:40,265 --> 00:06:41,765
Scene 5: Preparing for the Party

129
00:06:41,765 --> 00:06:44,810
The party is almost here!

130
00:06:44,833 --> 00:06:48,033
Yes, are you all set?

131
00:06:48,056 --> 00:06:51,323
The drinks are already chilled.

132
00:06:51,345 --> 00:06:54,012
Did you buy alcohol too?

133
00:06:54,035 --> 00:06:57,612
Yes, it's in the fridge.

134
00:06:57,636 --> 00:07:00,203
What about the food?

135
00:07:00,225 --> 00:07:03,425
I’ve already prepared the dishes.

136
00:07:03,448 --> 00:07:06,482
Is the room cleaned up?

137
00:07:06,505 --> 00:07:09,671
Yes, it's all tidy.

138
00:07:09,694 --> 00:07:12,071
How about the decorations?

139
00:07:12,095 --> 00:07:15,362
There are flowers on the wall.

140
00:07:15,385 --> 00:07:17,955
Are the chairs set up?

141
00:07:17,979 --> 00:07:20,612
No, not yet.

142
00:07:20,635 --> 00:07:23,902
Alright, I’ll arrange them.

143
00:07:23,925 --> 00:07:25,591
Thanks, I appreciate it.

144
00:07:25,614 --> 00:07:28,248
What about the table?

145
00:07:28,271 --> 00:07:30,481
Please wipe it down.

146
00:07:30,504 --> 00:07:32,238
Got it.

147
00:07:32,261 --> 00:07:35,461
I’ll set out the plates.

148
00:07:35,484 --> 00:07:38,417
Should I set out the chopsticks too?

149
00:07:38,440 --> 00:07:41,245
Yes, please do.

150
00:07:41,269 --> 00:07:44,072
I’ll put on some music too.

151
00:07:44,095 --> 00:07:46,828
Something soft and calm would be nice.

152
00:07:46,851 --> 00:07:49,518
Sure, I’ll find something.

153
00:07:49,542 --> 00:07:52,542
Should I open the windows?

154
00:07:52,565 --> 00:07:55,332
No, please keep it closed.

155
00:07:55,355 --> 00:07:57,488
Why's that?

156
00:07:57,511 --> 00:08:00,118
It's cold today, after all.

157
00:08:00,142 --> 00:08:01,475
Yeah, it is.

158
00:08:01,498 --> 00:08:04,587
That wraps up the preparations, then.

159
00:08:04,611 --> 00:08:06,111
Scene 6: Travel Plans

160
00:08:06,111 --> 00:08:09,199
We have time off starting tomorrow, don't we?

161
00:08:09,223 --> 00:08:13,790
Yes, I'm thinking of going somewhere.

162
00:08:13,813 --> 00:08:16,613
Where are you planning to go?

163
00:08:16,636 --> 00:08:19,769
I'm planning to visit Kyoto.

164
00:08:19,792 --> 00:08:22,004
That sounds nice.

165
00:08:22,028 --> 00:08:25,468
I'm thinking of hitting the hot springs.

166
00:08:25,491 --> 00:08:28,503
Who are you going with?

167
00:08:28,526 --> 00:08:31,611
I'm going with my family.

168
00:08:31,635 --> 00:08:35,035
Have you booked a hotel yet?

169
00:08:35,058 --> 00:08:38,492
Yes, I booked it last week.

170
00:08:38,515 --> 00:08:41,925
Are you planning to drive there?

171
00:08:41,948 --> 00:08:46,593
No, I'm taking the bullet train.

172
00:08:46,616 --> 00:08:49,074
Did you buy the tickets?

173
00:08:49,097 --> 00:08:53,031
No, not yet.

174
00:08:53,054 --> 00:08:56,487
You should buy them soon.

175
00:08:56,510 --> 00:08:59,845
I'm thinking of buying them tomorrow.

176
00:08:59,869 --> 00:09:03,069
Will that still be in time?

177
00:09:03,092 --> 00:09:06,533
I think it should be fine.

178
00:09:06,556 --> 00:09:09,996
I'm planning to go to the beach.

179
00:09:10,019 --> 00:09:14,076
The beach? Are you going to swim?

180
00:09:14,100 --> 00:09:18,466
No, I don't plan to swim.

181
00:09:18,489 --> 00:09:21,856
Then what are you planning to do?

182
00:09:21,879 --> 00:09:25,679
I'm planning to take photos of the ocean.

183
00:09:25,702 --> 00:09:28,237
Who are you going with?

184
00:09:28,260 --> 00:09:31,627
I'm going alone.

185
00:09:31,650 --> 00:09:35,130
Take care and have fun!

186
00:09:35,153 --> 00:09:36,822
Thank you.

187
00:09:36,845 --> 00:09:40,245
I'll bring back some Kyoto souvenirs for you.

188
00:09:40,268 --> 00:09:43,834
Oh, I can't wait!

189
00:09:43,857 --> 00:09:47,391
Yes, I hope you look forward to it.

190
00:09:47,414 --> 00:09:48,914
Scene 7: Symptoms of Illness and How to Respond

191
00:09:48,914 --> 00:09:51,847
You don't look well.

192
00:09:51,870 --> 00:09:55,003
I have a bit of a headache.

193
00:09:55,026 --> 00:09:58,260
You might have a fever.

194
00:09:58,284 --> 00:10:00,684
That could be it.

195
00:10:00,707 --> 00:10:04,508
You should head home early today.

196
00:10:04,531 --> 00:10:07,898
But I still have work to do.

197
00:10:07,921 --> 00:10:10,988
You shouldn't push yourself.

198
00:10:11,011 --> 00:10:14,978
I also have an important meeting tomorrow...

199
00:10:15,001 --> 00:10:18,569
It's better to rest before it gets worse.

200
00:10:18,592 --> 00:10:22,259
Should I take some medicine first?

201
00:10:22,282 --> 00:10:25,551
Yes, you should take some.

202
00:10:25,575 --> 00:10:29,115
Should I go to the hospital too?

203
00:10:29,138 --> 00:10:32,138
Yes, I think you should.

204
00:10:32,161 --> 00:10:35,494
Alright, I'll go to the hospital this afternoon.

205
00:10:35,517 --> 00:10:37,695
That would be best.

206
00:10:37,719 --> 00:10:41,286
It might snow outside, you know.

207
00:10:41,309 --> 00:10:44,075
It's going to be even colder this afternoon.

208
00:10:44,098 --> 00:10:47,665
Yes, it feels really chilly.

209
00:10:47,688 --> 00:10:50,722
You should dress warmly before you go.

210
00:10:50,745 --> 00:10:53,879
I should wear a thick coat, right?

211
00:10:53,902 --> 00:10:56,592
Yes, that would be best.

212
00:10:56,615 --> 00:10:59,983
Should I take a taxi to the hospital?

213
00:11:00,006 --> 00:11:03,058
The train might be better.

214
00:11:03,081 --> 00:11:05,415
Why do you say that?

215
00:11:05,438 --> 00:11:08,921
The roads might get congested because of the snow.

216
00:11:08,944 --> 00:11:10,420
Got it.

217
00:11:10,443 --> 00:11:13,057
Take care, then.

218
00:11:13,080 --> 00:11:14,813
Thank you.

219
00:11:14,837 --> 00:11:18,514
You should get plenty of rest tonight.

220
00:11:18,537 --> 00:11:20,937
Okay, I'll do that.

221
00:11:20,960 --> 00:11:22,460
Scene 8: How to Read Signs / Understanding Japanese Signs

222
00:11:22,460 --> 00:11:25,533
Take a look at that sign.

223
00:11:25,557 --> 00:11:28,652
What does it say?

224
00:11:28,676 --> 00:11:31,849
It says 'Stop'.

225
00:11:31,872 --> 00:11:34,039
What does that mean?

226
00:11:34,062 --> 00:11:38,628
It means you should stop here.

227
00:11:38,651 --> 00:11:40,298
Got it.

228
00:11:40,322 --> 00:11:43,995
There's something written over there too, isn't there?

229
00:11:44,019 --> 00:11:47,419
It says 'Do Not Enter'.

230
00:11:47,442 --> 00:11:51,777
That means you shouldn't go inside.

231
00:11:51,800 --> 00:11:53,838
That’s strict.

232
00:11:53,862 --> 00:11:58,195
Yes, because the inside of the factory is dangerous.

233
00:11:58,218 --> 00:12:02,430
They told me to wear a helmet.

234
00:12:02,454 --> 00:12:04,854
Who told you that?

235
00:12:04,877 --> 00:12:07,692
Someone from the factory did.

236
00:12:07,715 --> 00:12:11,401
Does that mean 'Protect your head'?

237
00:12:11,425 --> 00:12:14,258
Yes, I think so.

238
00:12:14,281 --> 00:12:17,756
What’s that red mark?

239
00:12:17,779 --> 00:12:21,383
It says 'Do Not Touch'.

240
00:12:21,407 --> 00:12:25,941
So it means don’t touch the machinery, right?

241
00:12:25,963 --> 00:12:28,597
Yes, it is.

242
00:12:28,620 --> 00:12:32,310
This one says 'No Smoking'.

243
00:12:32,333 --> 00:12:36,766
That means no smoking here.

244
00:12:36,789 --> 00:12:39,598
We can’t smoke here, then.

245
00:12:39,622 --> 00:12:43,468
Right, let’s smoke at the designated area outside.

246
00:12:43,491 --> 00:12:48,291
By the way, the manager said to come over.

247
00:12:48,314 --> 00:12:52,363
That means he wants you to come to the office, right?

248
00:12:52,386 --> 00:12:55,964
He also said to hurry.

249
00:12:55,988 --> 00:12:59,468
So that means 'Come back quickly'.

250
00:12:59,491 --> 00:13:02,225
Yes, let’s hurry.

251
00:13:02,248 --> 00:13:04,414
Got it.

252
00:13:04,437 --> 00:13:05,937
Scene 9: Helping with Cake Making / Helping with Cake Making

253
00:13:05,937 --> 00:13:09,373
We’re going to make a cake now.

254
00:13:09,397 --> 00:13:11,164
That sounds nice.

255
00:13:11,187 --> 00:13:15,063
We’ll follow the recipe book.

256
00:13:15,086 --> 00:13:17,501
Doesn’t that sound difficult?

257
00:13:17,525 --> 00:13:22,491
It’ll be fine if we follow what the instructor in the video says.

258
00:13:22,514 --> 00:13:25,685
Should I help too?

259
00:13:25,709 --> 00:13:29,842
Yes, please help after you wash your hands.

260
00:13:29,865 --> 00:13:32,080
I’ve washed them.

261
00:13:32,103 --> 00:13:36,958
Okay, crack the eggs into the bowl and mix them.

262
00:13:36,982 --> 00:13:39,115
Like this?

263
00:13:39,138 --> 00:13:44,938
Yes, then add the sugar and mix again.

264
00:13:44,961 --> 00:13:47,228
Should I add milk?

265
00:13:47,251 --> 00:13:51,451
No, let's make it without milk.

266
00:13:51,475 --> 00:13:54,213
Do we add water instead?

267
00:13:54,236 --> 00:13:58,134
Yes, we'll add a little water.

268
00:13:58,157 --> 00:14:00,853
What's next?

269
00:14:00,876 --> 00:14:04,410
After baking, we'll let it cool.

270
00:14:04,433 --> 00:14:07,366
How long should we bake it?

271
00:14:07,389 --> 00:14:10,522
We'll bake it as the instructions say.

272
00:14:10,545 --> 00:14:13,722
It says thirty minutes.

273
00:14:13,746 --> 00:14:17,146
Alright, let's bake it for thirty minutes.

274
00:14:17,168 --> 00:14:19,508
Should we spread some cream on it?

275
00:14:19,531 --> 00:14:23,582
No, we'll eat it without cream.

276
00:14:23,606 --> 00:14:26,139
That looks delicious!

277
00:14:26,162 --> 00:14:29,796
Let's eat it after chilling it in the fridge.

278
00:14:29,819 --> 00:14:32,312
I can't wait!

279
00:14:32,336 --> 00:14:36,022
I'll make some tea after cleaning up.

280
00:14:36,045 --> 00:14:38,292
Thank you.

281
00:14:38,316 --> 00:14:42,049
Do you take your tea without sugar?

282
00:14:42,072 --> 00:14:45,272
Yes, I drink it without sugar.

283
00:14:45,295 --> 00:14:46,795
Scene 10: How to Buy Souvenirs

284
00:14:46,795 --> 00:14:50,028
I'd like to buy some souvenirs.

285
00:14:50,051 --> 00:14:54,131
That shop over there is great for souvenirs!

286
00:14:54,155 --> 00:14:56,522
Is it far from here?

287
00:14:56,545 --> 00:15:00,712
No, it's just a five-minute walk.

288
00:15:00,735 --> 00:15:03,368
What’s tasty there?

289
00:15:03,391 --> 00:15:07,641
Their cookies are delicious if you're looking for sweets!

290
00:15:07,665 --> 00:15:10,432
Are the prices reasonable?

291
00:15:10,455 --> 00:15:14,055
Would you buy a lot if they’re cheap?

292
00:15:14,077 --> 00:15:18,211
Yes, I’d love to if they’re affordable!

293
00:15:18,234 --> 00:15:20,967
I think they’re probably cheap.

294
00:15:20,990 --> 00:15:25,071
We’ll know once we get there!

295
00:15:25,095 --> 00:15:29,138
Yeah, if we go now, it should still be open.

296
00:15:29,161 --> 00:15:32,628
We won’t go if it rains.

297
00:15:32,651 --> 00:15:35,784
It’s not raining right now!

298
00:15:35,807 --> 00:15:38,424
If it’s sunny, let’s go!

299
00:15:38,447 --> 00:15:41,182
Alright, let’s head out!

300
00:15:41,206 --> 00:15:44,775
Do they accept cards at that shop?

301
00:15:44,799 --> 00:15:48,599
Yes, they do take cards.

302
00:15:48,623 --> 00:15:52,640
If I don’t have cash, I’ll pay with a card.

303
00:15:52,663 --> 00:15:54,802
That works for me!

304
00:15:54,826 --> 00:15:59,492
If you’re not sure about the way, let me know!

305
00:15:59,515 --> 00:16:03,049
We can check the map on my phone.

306
00:16:03,072 --> 00:16:05,682
Smartphones are so handy!

307
00:16:05,706 --> 00:16:08,839
You’ll find it right away if you look it up.

308
00:16:08,862 --> 00:16:12,873
If we have time, I’d love to stop by a café too.

309
00:16:12,897 --> 00:16:16,630
That place over there has great coffee!

310
00:16:16,653 --> 00:16:19,720
If we go now, we should be able to get a seat.

311
00:16:19,743 --> 00:16:23,176
Yeah, let’s hurry a little.

312
00:16:23,199 --> 00:16:25,894
We’ll make it if we run!

313
00:16:25,917 --> 00:16:29,051
Just be careful not to trip!

314
00:16:29,074 --> 00:16:30,574
Scene 11: Developing Healthy Habits

315
00:16:30,574 --> 00:16:34,540
Have you been going to the gym lately?

316
00:16:34,563 --> 00:16:38,297
Yes, I’ve been going to lose weight.

317
00:16:38,320 --> 00:16:41,453
Do you run every day?

318
00:16:41,476 --> 00:16:45,543
Yeah, I can run much longer now.

319
00:16:45,566 --> 00:16:47,734
That’s amazing!

320
00:16:47,757 --> 00:16:51,195
I couldn’t run at all before.

321
00:16:51,219 --> 00:16:54,997
Do you try to exercise every day?

322
00:16:55,020 --> 00:16:59,154
Yes, I make sure to walk as much as I can.

323
00:16:59,177 --> 00:17:01,423
How’s your diet?

324
00:17:01,446 --> 00:17:05,079
I’ve been eating a lot of vegetables.

325
00:17:05,102 --> 00:17:07,869
Don’t you eat sweets?

326
00:17:07,892 --> 00:17:10,892
I try not to.

327
00:17:10,915 --> 00:17:14,248
I’ve gained weight recently.

328
00:17:14,271 --> 00:17:17,005
That’s because you don’t exercise.

329
00:17:17,028 --> 00:17:20,314
I can’t fit into my old clothes anymore.

330
00:17:20,338 --> 00:17:23,804
You should try to exercise a little.

331
00:17:23,827 --> 00:17:26,708
But I don’t have time.

332
00:17:26,731 --> 00:17:30,065
You could try waking up earlier.

333
00:17:30,088 --> 00:17:33,945
Have you gotten used to waking up early?

334
00:17:33,968 --> 00:17:37,934
Yes, I’ve been waking up at six.

335
00:17:37,957 --> 00:17:41,176
Alright, I’ll give it a shot.

336
00:17:41,200 --> 00:17:44,478
Have you learned to swim at the gym yet?

337
00:17:44,501 --> 00:17:48,114
No, I still can’t swim.

338
00:17:48,138 --> 00:17:51,622
Don’t give up—keep practicing.

339
00:17:51,645 --> 00:17:55,379
Okay, I’ll make sure to go to the pool.

340
00:17:55,402 --> 00:17:58,884
Be careful not to catch a cold.

341
00:17:58,907 --> 00:18:01,974
I will, thanks.

342
00:18:01,997 --> 00:18:05,855
I’ve been drinking a lot of water lately.

343
00:18:05,878 --> 00:18:08,478
That’s great for your health!

344
00:18:08,501 --> 00:18:11,668
Thanks to that, I’ve gotten healthier.

345
00:18:11,691 --> 00:18:13,191
Scene 12: A Terrible Day

346
00:18:13,191 --> 00:18:17,568
Today was the worst day ever.

347
00:18:17,591 --> 00:18:19,839
What happened?

348
00:18:19,863 --> 00:18:24,672
This morning, someone stepped on my foot in a packed train.

349
00:18:24,695 --> 00:18:27,662
Ouch, that must’ve hurt!

350
00:18:27,685 --> 00:18:31,565
Yeah, it really did.

351
00:18:31,589 --> 00:18:34,481
Did anything else happen?

352
00:18:34,504 --> 00:18:37,537
Someone pushed me from behind.

353
00:18:37,560 --> 00:18:39,993
That must have been tough.

354
00:18:40,016 --> 00:18:44,416
At work, my boss yelled at me.

355
00:18:44,439 --> 00:18:47,406
Did you make a mistake?

356
00:18:47,429 --> 00:18:51,696
Yeah, I messed up some documents.

357
00:18:51,719 --> 00:18:54,286
Did your boss call you in?

358
00:18:54,309 --> 00:18:57,842
Yeah, I was called into his office.

359
00:18:57,865 --> 00:19:00,498
Did he scold you harshly?

360
00:19:00,521 --> 00:19:04,555
Yeah, I got a long lecture.

361
00:19:04,578 --> 00:19:07,460
That’s rough. I’d be so down.

362
00:19:07,483 --> 00:19:11,616
On my way home, I got caught in the rain.

363
00:19:11,639 --> 00:19:14,606
Didn’t you have an umbrella?

364
00:19:14,629 --> 00:19:18,162
Mine got stolen.

365
00:19:18,185 --> 00:19:21,118
Wait, it got stolen?!

366
00:19:21,141 --> 00:19:26,151
Yes, my umbrella was stolen from the convenience store's umbrella stand.

367
00:19:26,175 --> 00:19:30,375
On top of that, I dropped my phone and it broke.

368
00:19:30,398 --> 00:19:33,249
Did someone bump into you?

369
00:19:33,272 --> 00:19:37,406
Yes, I was bumped into by a stranger.

370
00:19:37,429 --> 00:19:41,362
What a terrible day, huh?

371
00:19:41,385 --> 00:19:42,885
Scene 13: The Joy of Exercising

372
00:19:42,885 --> 00:19:46,218
It's such a beautiful day today.

373
00:19:46,241 --> 00:19:50,641
Exercising outside feels amazing.

374
00:19:50,664 --> 00:19:52,231
Yeah, it is.

375
00:19:52,254 --> 00:19:56,821
I love playing tennis.

376
00:19:56,844 --> 00:19:59,448
Me too!

377
00:19:59,471 --> 00:20:03,804
Working out on weekends is great for your health.

378
00:20:03,827 --> 00:20:08,694
Do you like watching sports too, Tanaka?

379
00:20:08,717 --> 00:20:10,517
Yeah.

380
00:20:10,540 --> 00:20:14,797
But I love playing sports the most.

381
00:20:14,820 --> 00:20:20,020
I'm not very good at running.

382
00:20:20,043 --> 00:20:22,443
That's okay!

383
00:20:22,467 --> 00:20:25,600
What matters is that we enjoy it together.

384
00:20:25,623 --> 00:20:28,707
Oh no!

385
00:20:28,730 --> 00:20:31,218
What happened?

386
00:20:31,241 --> 00:20:35,376
I forgot to bring my tennis shoes.

387
00:20:35,400 --> 00:20:37,200
Huh?

388
00:20:37,223 --> 00:20:40,461
You forgot to bring them?

389
00:20:40,485 --> 00:20:42,136
Yeah.

390
00:20:42,160 --> 00:20:45,407
I forgot to put them in my bag.

391
00:20:45,430 --> 00:20:49,076
Not having shoes is a problem.

392
00:20:49,099 --> 00:20:54,032
Did you know you can rent shoes at the front desk?

393
00:20:54,055 --> 00:20:55,630
Yeah.

394
00:20:55,654 --> 00:20:58,854
Yeah, I know you can rent them.

395
00:20:58,877 --> 00:21:01,010
That's good.

396
00:21:01,033 --> 00:21:03,930
I'll go rent some now.

397
00:21:03,954 --> 00:21:08,588
Oh, did you know Suzuki is coming today?

398
00:21:08,611 --> 00:21:12,905
No, I didn't know that.

399
00:21:12,928 --> 00:21:16,622
She'll be here soon.

400
00:21:16,645 --> 00:21:20,533
Suzuki is really good at tennis.

401
00:21:20,556 --> 00:21:21,956
Yeah.

402
00:21:21,979 --> 00:21:27,448
She's the best player among us.

403
00:21:27,471 --> 00:21:28,914
Yeah, it is.

404
00:21:28,938 --> 00:21:33,505
I get a little nervous practicing with her.

405
00:21:33,529 --> 00:21:38,896
Did you know Suzuki bought a new racket?

406
00:21:38,919 --> 00:21:42,339
No, I didn't.

407
00:21:42,362 --> 00:21:47,795
I'm excited to see her use it today.

408
00:21:47,818 --> 00:21:50,785
That sounds exciting!

409
00:21:50,808 --> 00:21:53,866
I can't wait to see it.

410
00:21:53,889 --> 00:21:58,668
Well, go rent your shoes quickly.

411
00:21:58,692 --> 00:22:00,325
Yeah.

412
00:22:00,348 --> 00:22:04,681
I'll make sure not to forget to pay at the front desk.

413
00:22:04,704 --> 00:22:08,602
We'll be using that court over there.

414
00:22:08,626 --> 00:22:10,603
Got it.

415
00:22:10,627 --> 00:22:12,760
I'll be right there.

416
00:22:12,783 --> 00:22:16,462
Be careful—running too fast is dangerous.

417
00:22:16,486 --> 00:22:18,219
Yeah.

418
00:22:18,242 --> 00:22:20,642
I will.

419
00:22:20,665 --> 00:22:22,165
Scene 14: Apologies and Communication for Being Late

420
00:22:22,165 --> 00:22:24,565
Sorry I'm late.

421
00:22:24,588 --> 00:22:28,040
I've been waiting for so long!

422
00:22:28,063 --> 00:22:31,711
The bus didn't come, so I was delayed.

423
00:22:31,734 --> 00:22:34,301
Was there an accident?

424
00:22:34,324 --> 00:22:38,857
The roads were jammed, and we couldn't move.

425
00:22:38,880 --> 00:22:42,280
I was worried, so I called you.

426
00:22:42,303 --> 00:22:47,472
My phone died, so I couldn't answer.

427
00:22:47,496 --> 00:22:50,463
That's tough, isn't it?

428
00:22:50,486 --> 00:22:53,943
Yeah, I was really panicking.

429
00:22:53,966 --> 00:22:58,703
I was a little upset since you didn’t contact me.

430
00:22:58,727 --> 00:23:01,760
I’m really sorry.

431
00:23:01,783 --> 00:23:05,229
I’m exhausted—let’s take a short break.

432
00:23:05,253 --> 00:23:09,147
That café over there is empty—let’s go in.

433
00:23:09,170 --> 00:23:11,857
I could really go for some coffee.

434
00:23:11,881 --> 00:23:16,315
It’s on me, so order whatever you’d like.

435
00:23:16,338 --> 00:23:18,271
Are you sure?

436
00:23:18,294 --> 00:23:21,542
I was late, so let me treat you.

437
00:23:21,565 --> 00:23:24,740
Well, if you insist, I won’t hold back.

438
00:23:24,763 --> 00:23:29,297
It was cold outside, so something warm sounds perfect.

439
00:23:29,319 --> 00:23:33,453
The rain came out of nowhere—it’s freezing now.

440
00:23:33,477 --> 00:23:37,371
I’m just glad I didn’t get wet.

441
00:23:37,395 --> 00:23:41,399
I had an umbrella, so I’m fine too.

442
00:23:41,423 --> 00:23:44,223
Are we still good for the movie time?

443
00:23:44,246 --> 00:23:48,179
We missed it, so we can’t watch it anymore.

444
00:23:48,202 --> 00:23:50,645
I’m really sorry about that.

445
00:23:50,669 --> 00:23:54,302
There’s another showing later, so it’s okay.

446
00:23:54,325 --> 00:23:56,302
That’s a relief.

447
00:23:56,325 --> 00:23:59,892
We’ve got time, so let’s take it easy.

448
00:23:59,915 --> 00:24:01,648
Yeah, it is.

449
00:24:01,671 --> 00:24:06,005
I’m not mad anymore, so don’t worry about it.

450
00:24:06,028 --> 00:24:07,528
Scene 15: Putting the Spiciness to the Test

451
00:24:07,528 --> 00:24:11,217
Does this dish taste good?

452
00:24:11,240 --> 00:24:16,313
I’ll have to try it first to see if it’s any good.

453
00:24:16,336 --> 00:24:19,376
It looks spicy, doesn’t it?

454
00:24:19,400 --> 00:24:24,053
Let’s ask the server how spicy it is.

455
00:24:24,077 --> 00:24:28,564
The server said it’s a little spicy.

456
00:24:28,588 --> 00:24:33,154
Not sure if we can handle it, though.

457
00:24:33,177 --> 00:24:36,511
Well, I’ll try a bite.

458
00:24:36,534 --> 00:24:38,312
How is it?

459
00:24:38,335 --> 00:24:41,193
It’s *really* spicy!

460
00:24:41,216 --> 00:24:43,787
Want to try some water?

461
00:24:43,811 --> 00:24:46,780
Yeah, I’ll give it a shot.

462
00:24:46,803 --> 00:24:48,677
You okay?

463
00:24:48,701 --> 00:24:53,381
It’s spicy, but I’ll try another bite.

464
00:24:53,404 --> 00:24:55,873
Do you actually *like* spicy food?

465
00:24:55,896 --> 00:25:00,663
I’m not even sure if I do or not.

466
00:25:00,686 --> 00:25:03,519
You’re sweating!

467
00:25:03,542 --> 00:25:07,792
It’s so spicy I can’t even tell if it’s hot anymore.

468
00:25:07,816 --> 00:25:10,624
Don’t push yourself, okay?

469
00:25:10,647 --> 00:25:15,825
By the way, do you know what kind of meat this is?

470
00:25:15,849 --> 00:25:20,082
Should we ask the server if it’s pork?

471
00:25:20,105 --> 00:25:24,238
The texture reminds me of chicken.

472
00:25:24,261 --> 00:25:27,742
Let’s check if it’s on the menu.

473
00:25:27,766 --> 00:25:31,333
Doesn’t look like it’s listed here.

474
00:25:31,356 --> 00:25:35,489
It’s delicious, so it doesn’t matter what kind of meat it is.

475
00:25:35,512 --> 00:25:38,479
Should we order dessert too?

476
00:25:38,502 --> 00:25:42,168
I’m curious if it’s sweet.

477
00:25:42,191 --> 00:25:45,161
I’ll try this cake.

478
00:25:45,185 --> 00:25:47,952
Do you have any idea how much it costs?

479
00:25:47,975 --> 00:25:51,208
I'll check the menu for the prices.

480
00:25:51,231 --> 00:25:53,898
Hope it's not too expensive.

481
00:25:53,921 --> 00:25:55,421
Scene 16: Proper Use of Honorific Language

482
00:25:55,421 --> 00:25:58,354
These sweets are so pretty!

483
00:25:58,377 --> 00:26:03,062
Yes, a client gave them to me.

484
00:26:03,086 --> 00:26:06,173
Are they from a famous shop?

485
00:26:06,197 --> 00:26:10,397
Yes, the president bought them for me.

486
00:26:10,420 --> 00:26:13,253
That's wonderful!

487
00:26:13,276 --> 00:26:17,156
Yes, I was so happy.

488
00:26:17,180 --> 00:26:20,746
Could I have one too?

489
00:26:20,769 --> 00:26:23,703
Of course, go ahead.

490
00:26:23,726 --> 00:26:25,692
Thank you.

491
00:26:25,715 --> 00:26:27,649
Thank you, I'll have one.

492
00:26:27,672 --> 00:26:30,145
How does it taste?

493
00:26:30,168 --> 00:26:32,968
It's really delicious.

494
00:26:32,991 --> 00:26:38,158
By the way, could you make some tea for the manager?

495
00:26:38,180 --> 00:26:41,260
Sure, I'll make some tea.

496
00:26:41,284 --> 00:26:46,729
It's rude to say 'ageru' when referring to the manager.

497
00:26:46,752 --> 00:26:49,018
Oh, right!

498
00:26:49,041 --> 00:26:50,522
I'm sorry.

499
00:26:50,546 --> 00:26:54,319
Please say, 'I'll make tea for you' instead.

500
00:26:54,342 --> 00:26:56,675
Okay, I understand.

501
00:26:56,698 --> 00:27:01,498
Did you feed your dog this morning?

502
00:27:01,521 --> 00:27:04,888
Yes, I fed him before I left.

503
00:27:04,911 --> 00:27:10,477
Then, could you water the office plants too?

504
00:27:10,500 --> 00:27:13,500
Sure, I'll do it now.

505
00:27:13,523 --> 00:27:17,857
Oh, by the way, my senior lent me a book.

506
00:27:17,880 --> 00:27:20,046
What kind of book is it?

507
00:27:20,069 --> 00:27:24,128
They told me it's a really good book.

508
00:27:24,151 --> 00:27:28,218
Could you take a photo of the cover later?

509
00:27:28,241 --> 00:27:31,610
Sure, I'll take a picture and send it to you.

510
00:27:31,634 --> 00:27:33,634
Thank you.

511
00:27:33,657 --> 00:27:38,132
Could you help me prepare for tomorrow's meeting?

512
00:27:38,156 --> 00:27:42,325
Of course, I'd be happy to help.

513
00:27:42,348 --> 00:27:44,836
That would be a huge help.

514
00:27:44,860 --> 00:27:46,360
Scene 17: Saving and Preparing for Moving

515
00:27:46,360 --> 00:27:51,093
You work part-time every day, don't you?

516
00:27:51,116 --> 00:27:55,349
Yes, I'm saving up to buy a house.

517
00:27:55,372 --> 00:27:59,306
How much does it cost to buy a house?

518
00:27:59,329 --> 00:28:02,495
It costs quite a lot.

519
00:28:02,518 --> 00:28:06,885
It's wonderful that you work for your family.

520
00:28:06,908 --> 00:28:11,397
I'm also saving up to go on a trip with my family.

521
00:28:11,421 --> 00:28:14,554
Where are you planning to go?

522
00:28:14,577 --> 00:28:17,510
We're planning to go to Hawaii.

523
00:28:17,533 --> 00:28:22,200
By the way, what are these scissors for?

524
00:28:22,223 --> 00:28:27,310
They're for cutting moving boxes.

525
00:28:27,333 --> 00:28:31,424
What's this big box for?

526
00:28:31,448 --> 00:28:35,497
It's for storing important items.

527
00:28:35,520 --> 00:28:39,404
You'll need quite a few things for moving.

528
00:28:39,427 --> 00:28:43,761
Yes, they're also useful for carrying clothes.

529
00:28:43,784 --> 00:28:49,263
How long does it take to get to the office from your new place?

530
00:28:49,286 --> 00:28:52,486
It takes about an hour by train.

531
00:28:52,509 --> 00:28:56,076
It's quite a long commute every day, isn't it?

532
00:28:56,099 --> 00:29:01,510
Yeah, but it's the perfect time to read books on the train.

533
00:29:01,533 --> 00:29:05,867
You bought books to study Japanese, right?

534
00:29:05,890 --> 00:29:10,890
Yes, but looking up words in the dictionary takes so much time.

535
00:29:10,913 --> 00:29:15,313
It always takes time to look things up at first, doesn't it?

536
00:29:15,336 --> 00:29:20,069
Lately, I've been exercising for my health too.

537
00:29:20,092 --> 00:29:24,959
Oh, so you bought new shoes for running?

538
00:29:24,982 --> 00:29:29,715
Yeah, they're great for working out.

539
00:29:29,738 --> 00:29:34,705
I barely eat anything to try and lose weight.

540
00:29:34,728 --> 00:29:37,261
That’s not good for you.

541
00:29:37,284 --> 00:29:40,559
Please eat to stay healthy.

542
00:29:40,582 --> 00:29:43,982
You're right. I'll be careful.

543
00:29:44,005 --> 00:29:48,461
You know, even sleeping uses energy.

544
00:29:48,484 --> 00:29:53,318
Well then, I'll make sure to get a good night's sleep to feel refreshed tomorrow.

545
00:29:53,341 --> 00:29:56,542
Yes, take it easy and rest well.

546
00:29:56,565 --> 00:29:58,809
Good night.

547
00:29:58,833 --> 00:30:00,333
Scene 18: Preparing for the Approaching Storm

548
00:30:00,333 --> 00:30:04,566
The sky's getting dark, isn't it?

549
00:30:04,589 --> 00:30:07,889
Yeah, it looks like it's about to rain any minute.

550
00:30:07,912 --> 00:30:11,124
The wind is picking up too.

551
00:30:11,148 --> 00:30:13,601
It feels like a storm is coming.

552
00:30:13,624 --> 00:30:17,998
We should get inside the building quickly.

553
00:30:18,021 --> 00:30:21,662
Alright, I'll go put away the stuff outside.

554
00:30:21,685 --> 00:30:25,255
The wind might break my umbrella.

555
00:30:25,279 --> 00:30:28,412
The wind is really strong, isn't it?

556
00:30:28,435 --> 00:30:31,869
It suddenly got cold.

557
00:30:31,893 --> 00:30:35,093
I might catch a cold like this.

558
00:30:35,116 --> 00:30:39,524
I'll go buy some hot tea over there.

559
00:30:39,547 --> 00:30:41,218
Thanks, I appreciate it.

560
00:30:41,242 --> 00:30:43,242
I got it.

561
00:30:43,265 --> 00:30:46,633
This tea looks really hot.

562
00:30:46,656 --> 00:30:49,623
Be careful when you hold it.

563
00:30:49,646 --> 00:30:53,447
Okay, I'll take a small sip.

564
00:30:53,470 --> 00:30:56,804
It looks warm and delicious.

565
00:30:56,827 --> 00:31:00,118
Yeah, it's really good.

566
00:31:00,141 --> 00:31:03,875
Oh, the sky is brightening up.

567
00:31:03,898 --> 00:31:07,031
It looks like the rain is stopping.

568
00:31:07,054 --> 00:31:10,465
Yeah, it's clearing up.

569
00:31:10,488 --> 00:31:13,724
That's a relief.

570
00:31:13,748 --> 00:31:16,604
Look, I think a rainbow might appear over there.

571
00:31:16,628 --> 00:31:19,707
I'll go check outside for a moment.

572
00:31:19,730 --> 00:31:22,530
Can you see a beautiful rainbow?

573
00:31:22,553 --> 00:31:26,687
No, it's not very clear yet.

574
00:31:26,710 --> 00:31:31,148
Now that I feel relieved, I'm suddenly feeling hungry.

575
00:31:31,171 --> 00:31:35,174
You look like you're about to cry from hunger.

576
00:31:35,198 --> 00:31:38,237
I'll go grab something to eat nearby.

577
00:31:38,260 --> 00:31:40,718
Take care.

578
00:31:40,742 --> 00:31:43,076
I'll be back soon.

579
00:31:43,099 --> 00:31:44,599
Scene 19: Overeating and Shoe Troubles

580
00:31:44,599 --> 00:31:48,599
I ate a bit too much for lunch.

581
00:31:48,622 --> 00:31:52,588
You always end up eating too much at buffets, don't you?

582
00:31:52,611 --> 00:31:57,219
I ate way too much. My stomach hurts so bad.

583
00:31:57,242 --> 00:32:00,609
Did you drink too much cold juice as well?

584
00:32:00,632 --> 00:32:05,499
Yeah, I had three glasses—way too much.

585
00:32:05,522 --> 00:32:09,331
And that last piece of cake was *way* too sweet.

586
00:32:09,355 --> 00:32:14,557
Plus, these shoes I wore today are killing me to walk in.

587
00:32:14,580 --> 00:32:17,713
Are they too small?

588
00:32:17,736 --> 00:32:21,775
No, the heels are just too high.

589
00:32:21,799 --> 00:32:25,799
Don’t push yourself—should we just take a taxi?

590
00:32:25,822 --> 00:32:30,876
Yeah, walking’s exhausting. Let’s grab a cab.

591
00:32:30,899 --> 00:32:33,710
We made it to the stationery store!

592
00:32:33,734 --> 00:32:36,934
This pen writes so smoothly!

593
00:32:36,957 --> 00:32:41,157
Seriously, and it’s *ridiculously* cheap.

594
00:32:41,180 --> 00:32:44,799
It’s so light and easy to use!

595
00:32:44,823 --> 00:32:48,438
I’ll take this red one, then.

596
00:32:48,461 --> 00:32:51,296
I’m gonna grab a book.

597
00:32:51,319 --> 00:32:55,653
Ugh, this book is so confusing.

598
00:32:55,676 --> 00:32:59,492
Yeah, way too many kanji.

599
00:32:59,515 --> 00:33:03,091
It’s way too hard for me to read.

600
00:33:03,115 --> 00:33:06,448
Want to pick an easier one?

601
00:33:06,471 --> 00:33:09,438
Yeah, that’d be better.

602
00:33:09,461 --> 00:33:14,227
This café’s seating is a little *too* dim.

603
00:33:14,250 --> 00:33:17,250
Makes it hard to read the book.

604
00:33:17,273 --> 00:33:20,673
I’ll turn on the lamp.

605
00:33:20,696 --> 00:33:23,904
Whoa, that’s *way* too bright!

606
00:33:23,928 --> 00:33:27,339
Okay, I’ll dim it a little.

607
00:33:27,362 --> 00:33:29,995
Perfect, just right.

608
00:33:30,018 --> 00:33:33,985
Is the music in here too loud?

609
00:33:34,008 --> 00:33:37,680
No, it’s nice and easy to listen to.

610
00:33:37,704 --> 00:33:40,377
Then let’s take this seat.

611
00:33:40,400 --> 00:33:42,933
Sounds good to me!

612
00:33:42,956 --> 00:33:44,456
Scene 20: Handling Return and Refund Issues

613
00:33:44,456 --> 00:33:48,623
The package I ordered online just arrived.

614
00:33:48,646 --> 00:33:51,312
Let’s open it right away!

615
00:33:51,335 --> 00:33:55,469
Oh no, a part is broken!

616
00:33:55,492 --> 00:33:59,225
And I paid so much for this...

617
00:33:59,248 --> 00:34:03,386
I was really looking forward to it too. Bummer.

618
00:34:03,410 --> 00:34:07,843
What do we do if it’s broken right out of the box?

619
00:34:07,866 --> 00:34:11,722
We should be able to return it to the store.

620
00:34:11,746 --> 00:34:15,642
I just called, but no one picked up.

621
00:34:15,666 --> 00:34:20,799
They’re not closed, so that’s weird.

622
00:34:20,822 --> 00:34:26,189
If we can’t reach them by phone, let’s email them.

623
00:34:26,212 --> 00:34:30,812
I emailed them, but still no reply.

624
00:34:30,835 --> 00:34:35,891
If they’re slow to respond, let’s give it a little more time.

625
00:34:35,915 --> 00:34:40,448
But I already waited a whole week for it to arrive!

626
00:34:40,471 --> 00:34:44,679
If you’re in a hurry, should we just cancel it?

627
00:34:44,703 --> 00:34:49,138
I’ve wanted this for so long, but I’ll let it go.

628
00:34:49,162 --> 00:34:55,562
Even if they send a replacement, the size might be wrong.

629
00:34:55,585 --> 00:35:00,427
It’d be a pain if it’s way too big for the room.

630
00:35:00,450 --> 00:35:06,017
I tried fixing it myself and read the manual, but I still don’t get it.

631
00:35:06,040 --> 00:35:10,510
If you’re stuck, I can read it for you.

632
00:35:10,533 --> 00:35:15,616
I’ve been studying Japanese, but I still can’t read this kanji!

633
00:35:15,639 --> 00:35:20,378
If you can't read it, just use your phone's dictionary.

634
00:35:20,402 --> 00:35:25,569
We promised to fix it together, but my friend never showed up.

635
00:35:25,592 --> 00:35:31,795
If my friend doesn’t come, should we just fix it by ourselves?

636
00:35:31,818 --> 00:35:37,427
I'm this upset, and you're laughing?

637
00:35:37,451 --> 00:35:41,684
If you feel like crying, go ahead and cry.

638
00:35:41,707 --> 00:35:47,907
I wanted to go out for a change of pace, but it's raining and I don’t have an umbrella.

639
00:35:47,930 --> 00:35:53,174
If I get wet, I’ll just go home and change clothes.

640
00:35:53,197 --> 00:35:57,444
I’m exhausted today, but I’m so shocked I can’t sleep.

641
00:35:57,468 --> 00:36:03,468
If you can’t sleep, how about drinking some warm tea?

642
00:36:03,491 --> 00:36:06,092
Okay, I'll do that.

643
00:36:06,116 --> 00:36:07,616
Scene 21: Phone Calls and Meetup Coordination

644
00:36:07,616 --> 00:36:10,783
Hello? Where are you right now?

645
00:36:10,806 --> 00:36:15,610
I just got to the station where we’re meeting.

646
00:36:15,633 --> 00:36:20,087
Sorry, I just rushed out of the house.

647
00:36:20,111 --> 00:36:23,544
Then you shouldn’t be here yet, right?

648
00:36:23,567 --> 00:36:27,534
Yeah, I should be about ten minutes away.

649
00:36:27,557 --> 00:36:31,490
I’ve been waiting right in front of the station this whole time.

650
00:36:31,513 --> 00:36:36,080
I’m really sorry—I’m running now.

651
00:36:36,103 --> 00:36:40,877
I was worried because you’re late, so I just called you.

652
00:36:40,900 --> 00:36:44,300
I just finally got on the train.

653
00:36:44,323 --> 00:36:48,656
If it’s an express, you should get off at the next stop, right?

654
00:36:48,679 --> 00:36:51,479
Yeah, I should be there soon.

655
00:36:51,502 --> 00:36:55,336
By the way, did you eat lunch yet?

656
00:36:55,359 --> 00:36:59,192
Yeah, I just ate before leaving.

657
00:36:59,215 --> 00:37:02,986
Then you shouldn’t be hungry, right?

658
00:37:03,009 --> 00:37:05,976
Nope, I’m full.

659
00:37:05,999 --> 00:37:09,565
I’m about to eat now.

660
00:37:09,588 --> 00:37:13,841
Oh, did the morning meeting end?

661
00:37:13,865 --> 00:37:17,632
Yeah, it just finished.

662
00:37:17,655 --> 00:37:20,422
Was the manager angry?

663
00:37:20,445 --> 00:37:23,941
No, he shouldn’t be.

664
00:37:23,964 --> 00:37:28,431
But I just got scolded over the phone.

665
00:37:28,454 --> 00:37:31,888
Ah, about being late, right?

666
00:37:31,911 --> 00:37:36,445
Once I get to the office, I’m going to apologize.

667
00:37:36,468 --> 00:37:40,547
If you apologize sincerely, it should be fine.

668
00:37:40,570 --> 00:37:42,203
I’ll do my best.

669
00:37:42,226 --> 00:37:45,797
I just finished the documents you asked for.

670
00:37:45,821 --> 00:37:49,191
Then there shouldn’t be any mistakes.

671
00:37:49,215 --> 00:37:53,348
I’m checking the data on my phone right now.

672
00:37:53,371 --> 00:37:55,470
It should be perfect.

673
00:37:55,494 --> 00:37:58,294
Yeah, no issues here.

674
00:37:58,317 --> 00:38:00,521
Please hurry and come.

675
00:38:00,544 --> 00:38:02,044
Scene 22: Preparations for Tanaka’s Wedding

676
00:38:02,044 --> 00:38:07,286
I heard Tanaka is getting married next month.

677
00:38:07,310 --> 00:38:09,000
Really?

678
00:38:09,024 --> 00:38:12,157
She seems so happy.

679
00:38:12,180 --> 00:38:13,747
Yeah.

680
00:38:13,770 --> 00:38:17,770
I heard her partner is really beautiful.

681
00:38:17,793 --> 00:38:21,959
I heard she’s quitting the company after getting married?

682
00:38:21,982 --> 00:38:25,422
No, I heard she’s not quitting.

683
00:38:25,446 --> 00:38:27,694
That’s great to hear.

684
00:38:27,718 --> 00:38:32,991
But lately, she’s been busy with wedding preparations.

685
00:38:33,014 --> 00:38:34,589
Yeah.

686
00:38:34,613 --> 00:38:38,080
I hear it's quite a hassle to prepare every day.

687
00:38:38,103 --> 00:38:42,282
They say there's going to be a party this weekend.

688
00:38:42,305 --> 00:38:45,116
I heard we might be invited too.

689
00:38:45,140 --> 00:38:49,540
No, it seems we're not invited.

690
00:38:49,563 --> 00:38:52,238
That's a little disappointing, isn't it?

691
00:38:52,261 --> 00:38:55,294
It sounds like it's just for family.

692
00:38:55,317 --> 00:38:57,207
I see.

693
00:38:57,231 --> 00:39:01,600
It seems the manager already knows about the wedding.

694
00:39:01,624 --> 00:39:03,190
Yeah.

695
00:39:03,213 --> 00:39:06,347
I heard they've already given their congratulatory gift.

696
00:39:06,369 --> 00:39:09,736
We should give something too.

697
00:39:09,759 --> 00:39:11,726
That sounds nice.

698
00:39:11,749 --> 00:39:16,824
By the way, they say it's going to rain starting tomorrow.

699
00:39:16,847 --> 00:39:20,913
Yeah, the weather seems pretty bad.

700
00:39:20,936 --> 00:39:24,870
I heard it's going to be even colder this weekend.

701
00:39:24,893 --> 00:39:29,026
It looks like Tanaka has caught a cold.

702
00:39:29,049 --> 00:39:33,049
Yes, I heard he just took some medicine.

703
00:39:33,072 --> 00:39:37,530
You should rest early and not push yourself.

704
00:39:37,553 --> 00:39:41,320
He said he went to the hospital this afternoon.

705
00:39:41,343 --> 00:39:45,635
The test results show it's not a serious illness.

706
00:39:45,659 --> 00:39:49,792
I heard his partner was relieved to hear that.

707
00:39:49,815 --> 00:39:52,020
That's a relief.

708
00:39:52,043 --> 00:39:53,543
Scene 23: Handling Urgent Personal Matters

709
00:39:53,543 --> 00:39:56,544
Excuse me, Manager.

710
00:39:56,567 --> 00:39:58,413
What's the matter?

711
00:39:58,437 --> 00:40:02,704
Would it be possible for me to leave early today?

712
00:40:02,727 --> 00:40:05,327
Is something wrong?

713
00:40:05,350 --> 00:40:08,916
My child suddenly came down with a fever.

714
00:40:08,939 --> 00:40:11,824
That must be tough.

715
00:40:11,848 --> 00:40:16,681
I need to go home now and take my child to the hospital.

716
00:40:16,704 --> 00:40:19,671
Please go home early.

717
00:40:19,694 --> 00:40:21,393
Thank you.

718
00:40:21,417 --> 00:40:25,350
I'll have someone else take care of your work.

719
00:40:25,373 --> 00:40:30,663
Could I ask Yamada to help with my tasks?

720
00:40:30,686 --> 00:40:33,970
Yes, let's have him do it.

721
00:40:33,994 --> 00:40:37,802
Would it be possible for me to take tomorrow off as well?

722
00:40:37,826 --> 00:40:40,099
Tomorrow too?

723
00:40:40,123 --> 00:40:46,123
My wife can't take time off, so I want to let her go to work.

724
00:40:46,146 --> 00:40:48,112
Got it.

725
00:40:48,135 --> 00:40:51,135
You can take tomorrow off.

726
00:40:51,158 --> 00:40:53,492
I'm really sorry about this.

727
00:40:53,515 --> 00:40:58,198
No, just make sure your child gets plenty of rest.

728
00:40:58,221 --> 00:41:02,702
As soon as I get home, I'll give my child some medicine.

729
00:41:02,725 --> 00:41:06,259
Don't push your child too hard, okay?

730
00:41:06,282 --> 00:41:10,215
Yes, I'll make sure they go to bed early tonight.

731
00:41:10,238 --> 00:41:14,005
I'll be waiting for your update tomorrow morning.

732
00:41:14,028 --> 00:41:18,322
I'll call you later to report on the situation.

733
00:41:18,345 --> 00:41:22,756
No, it's tough—just send me an email.

734
00:41:22,780 --> 00:41:27,355
Would it be alright if I took some work home?

735
00:41:27,378 --> 00:41:31,219
No, don't do any work today.

736
00:41:31,242 --> 00:41:34,097
Thank you so much.

737
00:41:34,120 --> 00:41:37,087
Please take care on your way home.

738
00:41:37,110 --> 00:41:39,080
Excuse me.

739
00:41:39,103 --> 00:41:41,074
Take care.

740
00:41:41,097 --> 00:41:42,597
Scene 24: How to Use Japanese Honorific Speech

741
00:41:42,597 --> 00:41:47,031
Has the president arrived at the office yet?

742
00:41:47,054 --> 00:41:50,621
Yes, they just arrived.

743
00:41:50,644 --> 00:41:54,377
Where are they now?

744
00:41:54,400 --> 00:41:58,093
They're in the meeting room.

745
00:41:58,117 --> 00:42:02,717
Have they read today's materials yet?

746
00:42:02,740 --> 00:42:06,940
Yes, they've already read them.

747
00:42:06,963 --> 00:42:10,129
What did they say about it?

748
00:42:10,152 --> 00:42:13,795
They said it was excellent.

749
00:42:13,819 --> 00:42:16,464
That’s great to hear.

750
00:42:16,487 --> 00:42:21,921
By the way, does the president often play golf?

751
00:42:21,944 --> 00:42:26,582
Yes, they often play golf on weekends.

752
00:42:26,605 --> 00:42:30,239
Are they going golfing tomorrow as well?

753
00:42:30,262 --> 00:42:34,428
No, they're taking the day off tomorrow.

754
00:42:34,451 --> 00:42:37,885
They seem a little tired lately.

755
00:42:37,908 --> 00:42:42,752
Yes, they’ll be resting at home tomorrow.

756
00:42:42,776 --> 00:42:47,469
Would the president like to try these sweets?

757
00:42:47,492 --> 00:42:51,226
Yes, they’d be happy to.

758
00:42:51,249 --> 00:42:54,782
Would they like some tea as well?

759
00:42:54,805 --> 00:42:59,172
No, they always drink coffee.

760
00:42:59,195 --> 00:43:02,090
Understood. I’ll prepare it.

761
00:43:02,113 --> 00:43:06,363
Is the manager in the meeting room now as well?

762
00:43:06,386 --> 00:43:10,474
No, the manager is away on a business trip.

763
00:43:10,497 --> 00:43:13,867
When will they return?

764
00:43:13,891 --> 00:43:17,326
They’ll be back tomorrow evening.

765
00:43:17,350 --> 00:43:22,116
Did they greet the president before leaving?

766
00:43:22,139 --> 00:43:25,776
Yes, they greeted them this morning.

767
00:43:25,800 --> 00:43:29,633
Ah, the client has arrived.

768
00:43:29,656 --> 00:43:33,889
Please show them to the reception room.

769
00:43:33,912 --> 00:43:36,312
Certainly.

770
00:43:36,335 --> 00:43:39,310
The president is waiting inside.

771
00:43:39,334 --> 00:43:40,834
Scene 25: Greetings and Project Introduction

772
00:43:40,834 --> 00:43:44,846
Nice to meet you. I look forward to working with you.

773
00:43:44,869 --> 00:43:48,069
Likewise, thank you for having me.

774
00:43:48,092 --> 00:43:54,532
Today, I’ll be explaining our new project.

775
00:43:54,555 --> 00:43:57,189
Please go ahead.

776
00:43:57,212 --> 00:44:00,849
I’ve reviewed the materials you sent in advance.

777
00:44:00,872 --> 00:44:02,769
Thank you.

778
00:44:02,793 --> 00:44:06,459
I think it’s a wonderful plan.

779
00:44:06,482 --> 00:44:09,325
I’m honored to hear that.

780
00:44:09,349 --> 00:44:14,315
I’ll send you a detailed quote by email later.

781
00:44:14,338 --> 00:44:16,305
I’ll be waiting for it.

782
00:44:16,328 --> 00:44:21,161
Our president asked me to pass along their regards.

783
00:44:21,184 --> 00:44:23,017
Thank you.

784
00:44:23,040 --> 00:44:25,276
Please send mine as well.

785
00:44:25,300 --> 00:44:30,385
Next time, I’ll bring samples of our new products.

786
00:44:30,408 --> 00:44:32,542
Thank you for going out of your way.

787
00:44:32,566 --> 00:44:34,465
Don’t mention it.

788
00:44:34,488 --> 00:44:39,421
I’m glad I could visit your office today.

789
00:44:39,444 --> 00:44:42,578
I’m happy we could meet as well.

790
00:44:42,601 --> 00:44:46,334
I’ll call you again tomorrow.

791
00:44:46,357 --> 00:44:49,324
What time will you call?

792
00:44:49,347 --> 00:44:52,227
I’ll call at 3 PM.

793
00:44:52,250 --> 00:44:54,543
Understood.

794
00:44:54,566 --> 00:44:57,737
Do you have any questions?

795
00:44:57,760 --> 00:45:00,328
Nothing at the moment.

796
00:45:00,352 --> 00:45:04,249
Well then, I’ll be signing off for today.

797
00:45:04,273 --> 00:45:06,744
Please take care on your way back.

798
00:45:06,767 --> 00:45:10,500
Thank you for taking the time out of your busy schedule.

799
00:45:10,523 --> 00:45:13,057
Hope to see you again soon.

800
00:45:13,080 --> 00:45:14,446
Yeah.

801
00:45:14,469 --> 00:45:18,036
